## Context
Source: Fable (claude-fable-5-1) and Astra (gpt-6-astra) review of the ruleset, 2026-11-01; reports in the session scratchpad, findings verified against main by the session. Astra finding, verifiable.

`skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md:251-255`: a comment-only hunk "is never a scope or
authorisation blocker, even under a path the brief marked protected (e.g. \"do
not edit `rapport/`\")". Scope is the author's call by right
(`rules/workflow.md` § Escalation protocol). A protected path means the author
withheld authorization; the gate overrides it for comments.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A hunk under a path the brief marked protected is scope_overflow whatever its kind; comment leniency applies only inside authorized scope
- [ ] A test pins the protected-path case
